<title>UK: RIO TINTO SHARES GAIN, TRACKING AUSTRALIA.</title>
<headline>RIO TINTO SHARES GAIN, TRACKING AUSTRALIA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in mining group Rio Tinto Plc rose to a four-week high on Friday, helped by gains in its Australian shares overnight, traders said.</p>
<p>By 0818 GMT, Rio shares wree up 29p or 2.83 percent at 10.55-1/2 stg, bucking a slightly weaker FTSE 100 index.  </p>
<p>Rio shares have gained eight percent this week, as analysts have also described the company as a late cycle play as commodity stocks are usually the last to enter a bull market when perceptions of inflation begin to creep up.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
